  "result": "Microsoft Word - 1257.doc (https://www.atcc.org/-/media/product-assets/documents/microbial-media-formulations/1/2/5/7/atcc-medium-1257.pdf?rev=2e25253395194bf58b7a7ac18c5c1933)\nciteturn34view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.atcc.org/-/media/product-assets/documents/microbial-media-formulations/1/2/5/7/atcc-medium-1257.pdf?rev=2e25253395194bf58b7a7ac18c5c1933\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 37\nL0@P0: ATCC medium: 1257 ETSA medium\nL1@P0: Trypticase Soy Agar (BD 211043)...40.0 g\nL2@P0: Yeast extract......................1.0 g\nL3@P0: Agar...............................4.0 g\nL4@P0: KNO3 ...............................0.5 g\nL5@P0: Sodium lactate, 60% syrup..........1.3 ml\nL6@P0: Sodium succinate...................0.5 g\nL7@P0: Sodium formate.....................0.5 g\nL8@P0: Hemin Solution (see below).........1.0 ml\nL9@P0: Distilled water..................924.0 ml\nL10@P0: Autoclave the above solution at 121C for 15 minutes. Cool to 55C. Aseptically\nL11@P0: add the following, freshly prepared, filter-sterilized solutions in the order\nL12@P0: listed:\nL13@P0: Menadione Solution (see below).....2.0 ml\nL14@P0: 4% L-Cysteine . HCl...............10.0 ml\nL15@P0: 0.5% Dithiothreitol (DTT).........10.0 ml\nL16@P0: 10% Glucose.......................10.0 ml\nL17@P0: 1% Sodium fumarate.................2.0 ml\nL18@P0: 4% Na2CO3 .........................10.0 ml\nL19@P0: Defibrinated sheep blood..........30.0 ml\nL20@P0: This medium solidifies very quickly and should be maintained at 50-55C while\nL21@P0: dispensing. Aseptically tube the sterile completed medium under an anaerobic\nL22@P0: atmosphere of 80% N2, 10% CO2, 10% H2. Plug the tubes with butyl rubber\nL23@P0: stoppers.\nL24@P0: A note of caution: Hydrogen gas can be explosive in the concentration used in\nL25@P0: preparing this medium. Gas tanks should be equipped with spark arrestors.\nL26@P0: Hemin Solution:\nL27@P0: KOH................................1.12 g\nL28@P0: 95% Ethanol......................100.0 ml\nL29@P0: Hemin............................200.0 mg\nL30@P0: Distilled water..................100.0 ml\nL31@P0: Dissolve KOH in water. Add ethanol and hemin.\nL32@P0: Menadione Solution:\nL33@P0: Menadione (Vitamin K3)............50.0 mg\nL34@P0: 95% Ethanol.......................50.0 ml\nL35@P0: Distilled water...................50.0 ml\nL36@P0: Dissolve menadione in ethanol; then add water. Filter-sterilize solution.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn34view1 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/antibiotics1968/39/5/39_5_652/_pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); \nFailed to fetch https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/antibiotics1968/39/5/39_5_652/_pdf: TimeoutError--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\npubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov (https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11594593/)\nciteturn34view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11594593/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\nL0: 【0†HHS Vulnerability Disclosure†www.hhs.gov】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOn an antibiotic, sarcidin, produced by Streptomyces n. sp. S. achromogenes - PubMed (https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/13061372/)\nciteturn34view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 1.4 years ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/13061372/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 352\nL0: \nL1: This site needs JavaScript to work properly. Please enable it to take advantage of the complete set of features!\nL2: \nL3: Clipboard, Search History, and several other advanced features are temporarily unavailable.\nL4: \nL5: 【0† Skip to main page content 】\nL6: \nL7: 【66†Image: U.S. flag†pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.go